 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Most of the world's nuclear weapons. Three leaders. One room, for the first time."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "The White House says Donald Trump, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin plan a joint meeting next week, on the sidelines of the APEC summit in Shenzhen, China. Reports put it on Thursday, November nineteenth, at the end of Trump's visit to China."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "On the agenda, per the White House: nuclear arsenals and the Iran war. New START, the last treaty capping American and Russian warheads, expired in February. A senior U.S. official says China's arsenal is growing fastest, and Beijing should join the talks."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "But no deal is expected. U.S. officials call it a starting point. The Kremlin calls the meeting extremely significant. Beijing only says it is in contact with the other sides, and it has long refused three-way nuclear talks."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will China join nuclear arms talks within a year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
